   and SC-182: the QA-checklist copy ("validate first-drop reorder", "reload the page and repeat") became a description of what the
   user does; the reorder-pipe colour picker went (a test knob; the parameter is named in the overview instead); the "Other Grid
   Demos" list went (the menu and Related cover it). OnLayoutChanged (GridSettings snapshot, fired from the header drop handler,
   GridControl.razor.cs ~12931) feeds a line under the grid with the new column order, so a drop has a visible result and the hook
   for saving user layouts is on show.
   2026-10-18: vocabulary written from GridControl.razor.cs (AllowColumnReorder ~675, ColumnReorderPipeColor ~713,
   OnLayoutChanged ~781, PersistenceKey ~794) and GridSettings.cs; rows checked against the source with scratchpad/vocabcheck.py.
